Marty Freitas writes...
> But when there character
> knows that there is nothing to gain it makes *NO* sense that he 
> would choke to death.  Do you postulate that they have no control
> over themselves once they begin to eat?  Or are you saying that 
> they are so stupid that they ignore the discomfort?

A minor point, but still - the idea with hack and other role-playing
games is that you ARE the character. You are his will, in control
of his actions (I exclude situations such as hallucination). If you
tell <him/you> to keep eating, it happens - so yes, the "Satiated" on
the status display is the warning and if you choose to ignore it, you
are ignoring his/your "discomfort" and (IMHO) accepting the possible
consequences.

